  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="qeramid-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">קרמיד</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">qrmyd</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">qeramid</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="pos">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen">m.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <form type="inflected">
               <orth type="inflected" xml:lang="jpa">קרמידין</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb">qrmydyn</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">geramidin</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="num">pl.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="qeramid-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>roof-tile</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>κεραμίς</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>κεραμίδος</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>[... ר' חייה בשם ר' יוחנן] בתחילה כדי רביעה ובסוף כדי שידחו 
                  <app>
                     <lem>פני הקרמיד</lem>
                     <rdg wit="#Ox1 Ox2">את הקרקע</rdg>
                  </app></quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">13,15</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 123: 6</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>R. Ḥiyya said in the name of R. Yoḥanan: At the beginning, sufficient to fructify; at the end, enough to wash the surface of the roof tiles. (Freedman / Simon I 108)</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">yBer 9,2 [72: 6]</bibl> (-)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Cf. <bibl type="modern">Jastrow II 1422a</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Fürst (1890) 210a</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Levy IV 381b-382a</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">AC VII 202a</bibl>. Cf. Krauss for other occurrences. For pl. cf. Yalq. <term xml:lang="jpa">כורמיזא</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">qwrmyzʾ</term> (attested i.a. in <bibl type="ancient">Targ. to Ex 21,18</bibl>, Jes 58,4 for Hebr. <term xml:lang="jpa">אגרוף</term>) Krauss renders also back to Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">κεραμίς</term>, but cf. Löw ad loc. Cf. <bibl type="modern">Levy, Targ I 389a</bibl>, who explains it as Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">χερμάδιον</term>.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Krauss, LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>569ab</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
      </body>
